<title>USA: US Treasury's sale of 52-wk bills seen at 5.72 pct.</title>
<headline>US Treasury's sale of 52-wk bills seen at 5.72 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's sale of $13.75 billion in 52-week bills on Thursday is expected to produce an average rate of 5.72 percent, traders said.</p>
<p>In when-issued trade at about 1240 EDT/1640 GMT, year-bills were quoted at 5.715.</p>
<p>The bidding deadline for the auction is 1300 EDT/1700 GMT. Results are expected around 1345 EDT/1745 GMT.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867 ))</p>
